{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Monitors source code files for changes and provides suggestions for code improvements, including identifying code smells, recommending design patterns, and highlighting best practices for better readability, maintainability, and performance",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "**/*.js",
      "**/*.ts",
      "**/*.jsx",
      "**/*.tsx",
      "**/*.vue",
      "**/*.css",
      "**/*.html"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code files for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any code smells such as duplicated code, long functions, large classes, or complex conditionals\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest applicable design patterns that could improve the code structure\n3. **Best Practices**: Check for adherence to best practices specific to the language/framework being used\n4. **Readability**: Suggest improvements for variable naming, code organization, and documentation\n5. **Maintainability**: Identify areas that could be refactored for easier maintenance\n6. **Performance**: Highlight potential performance optimizations without sacrificing readability\n\nProvide specific, actionable suggestions while maintaining the existing functionality. Be concise and prioritize the most impactful improvements."
  }
}